From: farjanatech damian-edition
Subject: [PATCH] rpi5cyw: bind Damian-edition direct Wi-Fi node RPI1060

Damian's ACPI contract already owns RPI0011 for the RP1 shared interrupt
provider. The Damian-edition UEFI therefore exposes direct CYW43455 SDIO as
ACPI\\RPI1060. Rebuild and re-sign the package after applying this patch.

--- a/package/rpi5cyw.inf
+++ b/package/rpi5cyw.inf
@@
-%DeviceDesc% = Device_Install.ndi, ACPI\\RPI0011
+%DeviceDesc% = Device_Install.ndi, ACPI\\RPI1060
--- a/installer/Install-RPi5-WiFi-Driver.ps1
+++ b/installer/Install-RPi5-WiFi-Driver.ps1
@@
-    $hardwarePattern = '^ACPI\\RPI0011(?:\\|$)'
+    $hardwarePattern = '^ACPI\\RPI1060(?:\\|$)'
@@
-            throw 'ACPI\RPI0011 was not found through PnP or CIM. Refusing to force-install the driver.'
+            throw 'ACPI\RPI1060 was not found through PnP or CIM. Refusing to force-install the driver.'
